---@field defaultRedirectUri? vercel.teams.TeamSamlDefaultRedirectUri The default redirect URI to use after successful SAML authentication.
---@field directory? vercel.teams.TeamSamlDirectory Information for the Directory Sync configuration.
---@field enforced boolean When `true`, interactions with the Team **must** be done with an authentication token that has been authenticated with the Team's SAML Single Sign-On provider.
---@field roles? vercel.teams.TeamSamlRolesMap When "Directory Sync" is configured, this object contains a mapping of which Directory Group (by ID) should be assigned to which Vercel Team roles and permissions, or an access group. Bare team roles are deprecated in favor of DirectorySyncRolesMapping.

---Information for the SAML Single Sign-On configuration.
---@class vercel.teams.TeamSamlConnection
---@field connectedAt number Timestamp (in milliseconds) of when the configuration was connected.
---@field lastReceivedWebhookEvent? number Timestamp (in milliseconds) of when the last webhook event was received from WorkOS.
---@field lastSyncedAt? number Timestamp (in milliseconds) of when the last directory sync was performed.
---@field state string Current state of the connection.
---@field syncState? vercel.teams.TeamSamlConnectionSyncState Controls whether directory sync events are processed. - 'SETUP': Directory connected but role mappings not yet configured. Events are acknowledged but not processed. - 'ACTIVE': Fully configured. Events are processed normally. - undefined: Legacy directory (pre-feature), treat as 'ACTIVE' for backwards compatibility.
---@field type string The Identity Provider "type", for example Okta.
---@field status string

